      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for erlotinib show substantial systemic exposure after oral dosing (AUC∞ about 10.2–15.2 µg·h/mL and Cmax about 1.1–2.6 µg/mL across single-dose and steady-state studies), consistent with its ~59% human F and supporting that a lipophilic heteroaromatic amine can be orally absorbed despite poor solubility.",
      "card_ids": ["C198","C195","C202","C197","C205","C34","C41","C70"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 solubility records show very low aqueous solubility for erlotinib (free base 7.2 µg/mL at pH 6.5; <20 µg/mL in pH 6.5 digestion medium) and vismodegib (1 µg/mL at pH 7; 0.4 µg/mL at pH 6.5–7.0), yet these molecules have human F values of ~59% and 31.8%, respectively; poor solubility alone is not affirmative evidence for F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C259","C266","C224","C240","C34","C41","C70","C62","C64","C167"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No query-specific solubility, permeability, or intestinal absorption measurement is available; L4 records are analog context only and do not provide direct evidence about the query's F.",
      "card_ids": ["C259","C224","C266","C252","C270","C227"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Low non-human F values (vismodegib monkey 13.4%, mouse 19.2%; dasatinib mouse 14–17%; 9-AC dog 10–13%; GSK monkey 7%; sildenafil rat 5.61%) are species-, dose-, and formulation-dependent and do not affirmatively establish F<20% in humans.",
      "card_ids": ["C83","C84","C148","C124","C149","C171","C143","C158","C173"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Bupropion's low or unknown values (~5%, 'low', 'unknown') come from a structurally dissimilar small aminoketone context and are not transferable to the query's large heteroaromatic scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C123","C152","C105","C114"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
